WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:19.385
Dawn broke and a fresh breeze blew through the branches of the fir trees, making the rustling sound that Heidi loved.

2
00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:22.643
It woke her, and she jumped out of bed.

3
00:00:22.644 --> 00:00:27.666
Her grandfather was already outside, washing Daisy and Dusky.

4
00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:34.482
Rosy clouds were floating in the clear morning sky, and the sun was coming over the mountains.

5
00:00:34.483 --> 00:00:36.996
"What, are you awake already?"

6
00:00:36.997 --> 00:00:40.493
asked Grandfather when Heidi came outside.

7
00:00:40.494 --> 00:00:45.279
Heidi ran to the trees and skipped delightedly under the waving branches.

8
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:54.150
Grandfather brought the goats out of their pen, and as soon as Heidi saw them, she ran and put her arms around their necks.

9
00:00:54.151 --> 00:00:57.293
Peter was whistling as he came up the path.

10
00:00:57.294 --> 00:01:02.650
His herd appeared first, and Heidi let Daisy and Dusky go join their friends.

11
00:01:02.651 --> 00:01:07.553
Peter wanted to talk to Heidi, so he pushed his way through the goats.

12
00:01:07.554 --> 00:01:11.487
"Can you come up the mountain with me?" he asked.

13
00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:17.508
"I can't, Peter. My friends from Frankfurt might come today," said Heidi.

14
00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:19.437
Peter wasn't happy.

15
00:01:19.438 --> 00:01:24.428
Heidi had said the same thing every morning since Clara's letter arrived.

16
00:01:24.429 --> 00:01:28.113
He left with the goats without saying good-bye.

17
00:01:28.114 --> 00:01:32.227
In Frankfurt, Heidi had learned to like being tidy,

18
00:01:32.228 --> 00:01:38.754
so after breakfast, she cleaned the table, put the dishes back in the cupboard, and tidied the hut.

19
00:01:38.755 --> 00:01:44.103
Then, a sunbeam, shining through the window, seemed to call her outside.

20
00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:48.242
She ran out and lay in the fresh, warm grass.

21
00:01:48.243 --> 00:01:53.696
Grandfather followed her, but was just in time to see her running down the mountain.

22
00:01:53.697 --> 00:01:57.798
"They're here!" Heidi shouted over her shoulder.

23
00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:00.550
"That's the doctor in front."

24
00:02:00.551 --> 00:02:04.668
She rushed on and greeted the doctor affectionately.

25
00:02:04.669 --> 00:02:07.125
The doctor's face brightened.

26
00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:10.011
He had not expected such a happy welcome.

27
00:02:10.012 --> 00:02:12.208
He shook her hand and said,

28
00:02:12.209 --> 00:02:16.179
"Take me to meet your grandfather and show me where you live."

29
00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.589
But Heidi did not move.

30
00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:21.611
She was looking down the mountain path, puzzled.

31
00:02:21.612 --> 00:02:26.576
"Where are Clara and Grandmamma?" she asked.

32
00:02:26.577 --> 00:02:30.011
"I'm going to disappoint you, Heidi," he replied.

33
00:02:30.012 --> 00:02:32.068
"I've come alone.

34
00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:34.655
Clara has been too ill to travel.

35
00:02:34.656 --> 00:02:38.966
But they will come in the spring, as soon as the days get warmer."

36
00:02:38.967 --> 00:02:42.093
For a minute or two, Heidi couldn't speak.

37
00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:44.567
She was greatly disappointed.

38
00:02:44.568 --> 00:02:49.557
When she looked up at the doctor, there was a lonely look in his eyes.

39
00:02:49.558 --> 00:02:53.644
It made her think he was just as disappointed as she.

40
00:02:53.645 --> 00:02:55.741
"It will be spring soon,"

41
00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:59.127
she said to cheer him up─and herself too.

42
00:02:59.128 --> 00:03:02.073
Hand in hand, they climbed to the hut.

43
00:03:02.074 --> 00:03:06.251
Grandfather put out his hand and welcomed the doctor warmly.

44
00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:12.084
The doctor seemed like an old friend because Heidi had talked about him so much.

45
00:03:12.085 --> 00:03:17.905
Grandfather had already brought the table out of the hut and had placed it in front of his seat.

46
00:03:17.906 --> 00:03:22.509
"Heidi," he said, "bring out what we need for lunch."

47
00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:28.592
To the doctor he said, "Our food is simple, but the dining room is fine!"

48
00:03:28.593 --> 00:03:36.164
As Heidi set the table, running back and forth, the doctor seemed to notice the beautiful surroundings for the first time.

49
00:03:36.165 --> 00:03:40.647
"Everything will taste extra good up here," he said.

50
00:03:40.648 --> 00:03:47.957
They sat down to eat, and the doctor explained all about Clara's illness and Herr Sesemann's suggestion that he visit.

51
00:03:47.958 --> 00:03:51.729
While they were eating, a man arrived carrying a chest.

52
00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.513
The doctor smiled.

53
00:03:53.514 --> 00:03:58.629
"These are presents from Clara and Grandmamma," he explained.

54
00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:05.962
Heidi was thrilled, and among all the wonderful gifts was the package of coffee that had been promised for Grannie.

55
00:04:05.963 --> 00:04:12.871
There was also a packet of tobacco for Grandfather, which he accepted from the doctor with a grin.

56
00:04:12.872 --> 00:04:19.393
As the afternoon ended, Grandfather walked down the mountain to help the doctor find a room in Dorfli.

57
00:04:19.394 --> 00:04:26.690
Both smoked their pipes, and Heidi went too, to deliver the coffee to Grannie.
